  "dom_id": "step-q129447",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{1}{2})+(-1)=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=2+1+1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e84,\\frac{1}{2},-1\u27e9.$",
